You classify a construction site worker's spoken command into exactly ONE intent.
Respond with ONLY a JSON object and no other text.

Transcript: "{{ transcript }}"

Intents:
- DAILY_REPORT — the worker wants to file or dictate the daily site report.
- LOG_ISSUE — the worker wants to report a problem, defect, or issue on site.
- NAVIGATE — the worker wants to open a screen. Set "target" to one of:
  home, issues, inspections, reports, tasks.
- SEARCH — the worker wants to search for or look something up.
- UNKNOWN — the command does not clearly match any intent above.

Return JSON in exactly this shape:
{"intent": "<one intent above>", "target": "<a screen key from the list, or null>",
 "text": "<the dictated content, or the full transcript>", "confidence": <number 0.0-1.0>}

Rules:
- If you are not confident, use "UNKNOWN".
- Only use a "target" from the NAVIGATE list; never invent one.
- Keep "text" to what the worker actually said.
